arize the text's findings on FMT/ICI trials (Phase 1 melanoma, Phase 2 uncontrolled CRC) and the explicit statement that large RCTs are needed.\n-   **auxiliary_material:** Mechanisms of microbiome-ICI interaction (Fn, Pa, etc.) mentioned in the text which explain *why* interventions are being tested, even if Phase III is missing.\n-   **remaining_gap:** The specific data from a completed large Phase III RCT is missing. The text confirms this is an open area.\n-   **outline_action:** Use this text to justify the need for Phase III trials and to summarize the current lower-level evidence (Phase 1/2) while explicitly stating the lack of Phase III confirmation.\n\n**Refining Constraints:**\n-   \"Do not call the whole gap fulfilled while a stated success criterion remains open.\" -> The success criterion is \"Return directly relevant evidence or state why the gap remains unresolved.\" I can state why it remains unresolved using this text. But the *status* of the gap (existence of Phase III evidence) is unmet by this text.\n-   \"Refer to the paper as 'this study' or 'the authors'...\" -> It's a review article. I should refer to it as \"this review\" or \"the authors\". The prompt says \"Refer to the paper as 'this study' or 'the authors' unless its identity is explicitly given\". The text says \"In this review...\". I will use \"this review\" or \"the authors\".\n-   \"Do not infer the paper's identity from its reference list.\" -> Okay.\n-   \"Keep each finding attached to the study...\" -> Okay.\n-   \"A study-design label is used only when explicitly stated.\" -> The text states \"Phase 1 clinical study\", \"phase 2 study\", \"without a control group\".\n-   \"Review-reported original studies remain usable writing material with their review attribution; do not claim the original full text was read.\" -> I must attribute findings to the review's reporting of other studies (e.g., \"the authors cite Phase ","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs